# A generic local function used as a value at two types (Semantics ch. 4: `fn` lines in a
# block; Type System ch. 5, "A local `let` generalizes": a local function with no signature is generalized as a `let`
# is, so each use takes its own instance). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering
# branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Both: fn [Nat], [Text] -> Text
fn Both ns, ts:
    fn Same x = x
    "{Len (Each ns, Same)} {Concat (Each ts, Same)}"

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Both [[1, 2]], [["a", "b"]]}")                # 0
